</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Frequent loss of heterozygosity for loci on chromosome 8p in hepatocellular carcinoma, colorectal cancer, and lung cancer</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1992</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>5368</fpage><lpage>5372</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1356616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Roz</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Holland</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Porter</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Scully</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Speight</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Thakker</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Deletion mapping defines three discrete areas of allelic imbalance on chromosome arm 8p in oral and oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinomas</article-title><source>Genes Chromosomes Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>353</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9408750</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1098-2264(199712)20:4&#x0003c;347::AID-GCC5&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Do</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurst</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Khoo</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname